# Jira MCP

Use Jira MCP as the source of truth for issue details.

When the user references an issue such as `KAN-1`:

- Fetch the issue from Jira before implementation.
- Do not rely only on issue titles mentioned in chat.
- Read description, acceptance criteria, and status.
- If Jira requirements conflict with chat instructions, ask for clarification.
- Do not update Jira issue status unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not create Jira comments unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not modify other Jira issues while implementing the current issue.

Before coding, respond with:

- Goal
- Implementation plan
- Files to create or modify
- Any assumptions

Then wait for approval if the user asked to review the plan first.
